  },
  "question": {
    "text": "The mean and standard deviation of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn></math>&nbsp;observations are&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;respectively. It was noticed that two of these observations&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>12</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn></math>&nbsp;were wrongly recorded. If&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#963;</mi></math>&nbsp;is the standard deviation of the data after omitting the two wrong observations from the data, then&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>38</mn><msup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;is equal to _______."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "238",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given,</p><p>Wrong mean&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math></p><p>Wrong standard deviation&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Now mean ig given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mn>40</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8721;</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1200</mn></math></p><p>Variance is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>&#8721;</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mn>40</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mn>30</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#8721;</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>925</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>37000</mn></math></p><p>New sum of mean&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8721;</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1200</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>12</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>1178</mn></math></p><p>So, new mean&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>&#956;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1178</mn><mn>38</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>31</mn></math></p><p>Now new variance&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8721;</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>37000</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>10</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>12</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>36756</mn></math></p><p>So, new S.D.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>&#39;</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mn>36756</mn><mn>38</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>31</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mi>&#963;</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>36756</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>31</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>38</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>38</mn><msup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>38</mn><msup><mi>&#963;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>238</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
  }
